        "documentation": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "From `\"AudioTools/CoreAudio/AudioEffects/PitchShift.h\"`  \n@brief Variable speed ring buffer with 180-degree phase shifting  \nAdvanced buffer implementation that reads with 0° and 180° phase offsets and blends the results to prevent overrun artifacts. This technique reduces audio artifacts when read and write pointers collide by cross-fading between two read positions that are 180° apart (half buffer apart).  \nBased on the algorithm described at:  \nhttps://github.com/YetAnotherElectronicsChannel/STM32_DSP_PitchShift  \n@ingroup buffers  \n@tparam T The sample data type (typically int16_t or float)"
        },
