        "documentation": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "From `\"AudioTools/CoreAudio/AudioEffects/PitchShift.h\"`  \n@brief Very Simple Buffer implementation for Pitch Shift  \nThis buffer writes samples at constant speed but allows reading at variable speed to achieve pitch shifting. The reading speed is controlled by the increment parameter.  \nWhen read and write pointers overlap, some audio artifacts (noise) may be audible.  \n@warning This is a basic implementation that may produce audible artifacts during pointer overruns. For better quality, consider using VariableSpeedRingBuffer180 or VariableSpeedRingBuffer.  \n@ingroup buffers  \n@tparam T The sample data type (typically int16_t or float)"
        },
