          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "From `\"freertos/portable.h\"`  \nUsed to define multiple heap regions for use by heap_5.c. This function must be called before any calls to pvPortMalloc() - not creating a task,  \nqueue, semaphore, mutex, software timer, event group, etc. will result in pvPortMalloc being called.  \npxHeapRegions passes in an array of HeapRegion_t structures - each of which defines a region of memory that can be used as the heap. The array is terminated by a HeapRegions_t structure that has a size of 0. The region with the lowest start address must appear first in the array."
        },
